  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 25 July 2007, the retention of a roof extension  measuring 2.6m depth by 2.6m wide by 3.1m high and two roof lights fronting the highway, was not lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development exceeds the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Classes A and B of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the volume of the roof extension including the existing single storey rear extension and garden shed is above the permitted development limit for a terraced house not in a conservation area and the rooflights on the front plane of the roof project beyond the existing roof slope which fronts a highway.\r\n"
